  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down (5 minutes)</title>
<title>Student Activity</title>
<para>Thomasina used a quadratic data set to create a curve of best fit for her data. Then she accidentally spilled paint on her paper and lost some of the entries in the table.</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-desmos-gc" data-bottom="-100" data-equations="[&quot;y=-.34x^2+30.31x+18.45&quot;]" data-left="-10" data-right="100" data-schema-version="1.0" data-top="800"/>
<para>(Students were provided access to Desmos)</para>
<para>She needs to work backward to fill in the missing entries in her data set. Use the curve of best fit she created to complete the table.</para>
<table class="os-raise-skinnytable">
<thead>
    <row>
      <entry><emphasis>
        \(x_1\)
      </emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>
        \(y_1\)
      </emphasis></entry></row>
    </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry>
        6
      </entry>
      <entry/>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry/>
      <entry>
        452.06
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry/>
      <entry>
        632.24
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        58.2
      </entry>
      <entry/>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry/>
      <entry>
        176.12
      </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>

<para>Write down your answers, then select the <emphasis>solution </emphasis>button to compare your work.</para>
<para><emphasis>Answers:</emphasis></para>
<table class="os-raise-skinnytable">
